Conclusion: Yes, there was an assembly (public meeting) with participants, and it appears peaceful (no evidence of disturbance). So scope = yes.

Interference: Did a governmental act or omission interfere with the applicant's freedom of assembly? The fine imposed by district court for lack of prior authorization interferes. So facts: F013 (fine imposed), F014 (for breach of rules of conducting public manifestations), F015 (lack of prior authorisation), plus perhaps F016-18 (appeal process). So at least F013-F015. Conclusion: yes, there was interference.

